@Robertzu43, I read all six findings in [your review of e9df5cb](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/53#pullrequestreview-5560453685). I reproduced their integration behavior in an isolated archive of exact SHA `e9df5cbfd5c2cfbb19698d46bb957b8561920e66`, using Node **22.22.3**: **14 reproduction assertions confirmed the failures**. This is author reproduction evidence, not a fix or independent acceptance.

1. **300 ms phone skew:** confirmed `source-after-server-receipt`/`unknown`. The actual snapshot endpoint owns capture acceptance and server freshness; the app should consume that authoritative contract instead of reclassifying it with this provisional rule.
2. **Uncertainty near now:** confirmed a 5 s-old point with 30 s uncertainty produces minimum age -25 s and `unknown`. The app will preserve the server's returned age/freshness and their limits, without applying this second source-time uncertainty calculation.
3. **History overlap/null uncertainty:** confirmed both 3 s cadence with 2 s uncertainty and an older null-uncertainty point remove the selected latest fact. The backend's retained latest snapshot is the integration source; this history selector will not sit in front of it.
4. **Contact permission:** confirmed remote-driver permission `unknown` overrides a `recent` location. The contact view must rely on authorized server map/status facts; local capture permission belongs to the observing driver device and cannot gate a remote contact's valid snapshot.
5. **Backend vocabulary/shape:** confirmed whole-call TypeError for pending/claimed/authorized/rejected/unknown/unavailable job states, missing uncertainty and backend `accuracy`. Lane45's typed adapter will consume actual published response shapes; unavailable notification facts must not hide the independent location panel. This provisional schema will not be broadened into another backend contract.
6. **Resume clocks:** confirmed paused monotonic time plus advanced wall time makes the projection unknown. On resume the app should refresh server facts while retaining clearly timestamped last observations. Any optional between-poll age is derived once from returned server age and elapsed client time; it never creates a new observation, fills a sleep gap or resets a server deadline.

**Proposed disposition: PARK this preparatory module and keep PR #53 draft/HOLD; exclude it from the complete-app screens.** Preserve the branch, tests and earlier evidence at their exact SHA. The shared foundation is a separate branch/PR #56; it will consume `/snapshot` and the forthcoming `/status` only after the API owner publishes the real contract through lanes41/45. `/status` is a reported planned dependency, not an implemented route at inspected backend `ebc8fb1`. No provisional deadline/response/notification values will be invented to satisfy these inputs. I have sent the integration consequences to Brain and the API/runtime owners.

Please confirm agreement with this parking/replacement disposition. Until then these six integration findings remain open; no author resolution, merge or issue #22 completion is claimed. No source changes or empty review commits were made to the frozen projection branch. Human/device capability and comprehension gates remain unperformed.

